{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a transition-metal-free, visible-light photoredox-catalyzed method for the remote borylation of unactivated C(sp3)-H bonds. The reaction is enabled by a 1,5-hydrogen atom transfer (HAT) process from an amidyl radical, generated by the reductive cleavage of hydroxamic acid derivatives using Eosin Y as an organic photocatalyst. The method demonstrates broad substrate scope, including primary, secondary, and tertiary C-H bonds, and is applicable to complex molecules and gram-scale synthesis.",
